00:01:09.575 --> 00:01:10.558
- Showtime.

00:01:10.558 --> 00:01:13.718
I'm a very spiritual person,
and I follow my spirit,

00:01:13.718 --> 00:01:16.203
and I do what my spirit tells me to do.

00:01:16.203 --> 00:01:18.256
You know, and I don't have a set ...

00:01:18.256 --> 00:01:20.237
Like "Oh, I want to play
this type of character,

00:01:20.237 --> 00:01:22.003
"and I won't play that type of character."

00:01:22.003 --> 00:01:24.170
I'm receptive to anything.

00:01:25.714 --> 00:01:28.857
And when the right thing
comes along, if it's serious,

00:01:28.857 --> 00:01:32.172
if it's funny, if it's silly, if it's ...

00:01:32.172 --> 00:01:33.876
But see I'm, put it this way,

00:01:33.876 --> 00:01:36.459
I just do whatever makes me ...

00:01:37.503 --> 00:01:39.142
I get the most ...

00:01:39.142 --> 00:01:42.053
Gratification from, as
an artist, you know.

00:01:42.053 --> 00:01:44.485
I do music albums, and
nobody buys my records,

00:01:44.485 --> 00:01:47.313
I do them because I love
making music, you know,

00:01:47.313 --> 00:01:49.045
and that's the same way I'm about movies.

00:01:49.045 --> 00:01:50.597
I don't make movies because ...

00:01:50.597 --> 00:01:53.111
I don't go into it
thinking, "Let me do this,

00:01:53.111 --> 00:01:54.652
"because then people will come," or

00:01:54.652 --> 00:01:56.183
"How much will a movie make," and

00:01:56.183 --> 00:01:57.918
"I'm trying to make the audience do that."

00:01:57.918 --> 00:02:00.791
I do what feels right for me.

00:02:00.791 --> 00:02:02.623
I knew I wanted to be in show business,

00:02:02.623 --> 00:02:05.844
and I just happened to luck
out and things happened.

00:02:05.844 --> 00:02:07.504
I think you know ...

00:02:07.504 --> 00:02:10.713
You know what you're supposed to do.

00:02:10.713 --> 00:02:12.264
Deep down inside, I think everybody does,

00:02:12.264 --> 00:02:14.854
and a lot of people
just don't go after it.

00:02:14.854 --> 00:02:16.898
You know, like most
people start out, they say

00:02:16.898 --> 00:02:18.860
"I want to be a this,
but I'm going to get that

00:02:18.860 --> 00:02:21.021
"to make sure I have
something to fall back on."

00:02:21.021 --> 00:02:23.307
And what you're doing is you're
setting yourself to fail,

00:02:23.307 --> 00:02:24.300
'cause you're going,

00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:26.153
"There's a possibility
that I'm 'a fall back."

00:02:26.153 --> 00:02:28.802
And when you put that out
there, then you fall back,

00:02:28.802 --> 00:02:30.319
but if you just say, "Hey,
this is what I want to do,"

00:02:30.319 --> 00:02:32.305
and you go do it, you
usually get your stuff

00:02:32.305 --> 00:02:34.756
the way you want it, man.

00:02:34.756 --> 00:02:37.724
I don't think I'll ever
give anybody any advice.

00:02:37.724 --> 00:02:38.557
- [Interviewer] Almost all the advice

00:02:38.557 --> 00:02:40.963
I've been given was wrong.

00:02:40.963 --> 00:02:43.347
- We shouldn't follow advice.

00:02:43.347 --> 00:02:44.914
- [Interviewer] That's our advice.

00:02:44.914 --> 00:02:48.513
- (Laughs) Take our advice,
don't follow advice.

00:02:48.513 --> 00:02:50.273
'Cause everybody's life is different,

00:02:50.273 --> 00:02:52.072
everybody's got different ...

00:02:52.072 --> 00:02:53.055
If something works for John,

00:02:53.055 --> 00:02:55.818
doesn't mean it's going to work for me.

00:02:55.818 --> 00:02:57.633
So do your own thing.

00:02:57.633 --> 00:02:59.289
And you kids out there, do what you want,

00:02:59.289 --> 00:03:00.919
and if your parents want
you to do something else,

00:03:00.919 --> 00:03:03.333
do what you want, 'cause
nine out of ten times

00:03:03.333 --> 00:03:04.359
you'll be right.

00:03:04.359 --> 00:03:05.801
And if you become a bum, hey,

00:03:05.801 --> 00:03:09.683
we told you not to take
advice, right? (laughs)

00:03:09.683 --> 00:03:13.781
My whole family is funny, I
have a really funny, funny

00:03:13.781 --> 00:03:15.757
fam, like we're ...

00:03:15.757 --> 00:03:18.489
The whole family can tell jokes, and ...

00:03:18.489 --> 00:03:20.099
To the dozens and all that,

00:03:20.099 --> 00:03:23.544
so we're always really
funny around the house.

00:03:23.544 --> 00:03:27.622
When I realized I wanted to be
a comedian was Richard Pryor.

00:03:27.622 --> 00:03:31.009
That's who was like, "Oh that's
what I want to be," so ...

00:03:31.009 --> 00:03:34.029
(applause)

00:03:34.029 --> 00:03:35.529
It's 1976 I think,

00:03:36.818 --> 00:03:40.415
it was the album he put out
called That Nigger's Crazy.

00:03:40.415 --> 00:03:43.380
And I remember just sitting
and listening to it,

00:03:43.380 --> 00:03:46.617
over and over and over and
over and over and over,

00:03:46.617 --> 00:03:48.556
and that was kind of where it started.

00:03:48.556 --> 00:03:51.296
That's where I realized what
I was, what I wanted to do.

00:03:51.296 --> 00:03:54.177
Ultimately, I just want to
be known as a person who

00:03:54.177 --> 00:03:56.931
wants to make people feel good.

00:03:56.931 --> 00:03:58.768
- [Narrator] It was
Eddie's genius for comedy

00:03:58.768 --> 00:03:59.920
that caught the eye of Hollywood,

00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:01.869
and turned Eddie Murphy the comedian

00:04:01.869 --> 00:04:03.878
into Eddie Murphy the movie star.

00:04:03.878 --> 00:04:08.086
(crash)
(groan)

00:04:08.086 --> 00:04:09.738
- What's happening, Luther?

00:04:09.738 --> 00:04:11.009
I'm sorry about the door, man.

00:04:11.009 --> 00:04:11.842
Did that hurt?

00:04:11.842 --> 00:04:13.950
It looked real painful
when you slammed into it.

00:04:13.950 --> 00:04:16.876
I think everybody has talents,
and all you have to do

00:04:16.876 --> 00:04:20.489
is find what your talents
are, and put focus into it.

00:04:20.489 --> 00:04:24.915
And when I was 15, I knew I was
going to be in show business,

00:04:24.915 --> 00:04:26.422
and I knew that's what I was going to do.

00:04:26.422 --> 00:04:28.392
I'm just a comedian, you know.

00:04:28.392 --> 00:04:31.142
I don't really listen to critics.

00:04:32.024 --> 00:04:33.315
That's coming from a person who gets ...

00:04:33.315 --> 00:04:34.598
I guess 'cause I get criticized a lot,

00:04:34.598 --> 00:04:36.490
you can't listen to it.

00:04:36.490 --> 00:04:38.627
I just do what I do, you know?

00:04:38.627 --> 00:04:40.524
I can't, when they say good things,

00:04:40.524 --> 00:04:42.119
I don't sit around and
say, "Yeah, that's right."

00:04:42.119 --> 00:04:43.313
When they say bad things ...

00:04:43.313 --> 00:04:44.207
- [Interviewer] Do you read everything?

00:04:44.207 --> 00:04:46.045
- I read everything they say.

00:04:46.045 --> 00:04:47.038
- [Interviewer] Do you
have a clipping service,

00:04:47.038 --> 00:04:48.311
so you read everything?

00:04:48.311 --> 00:04:50.383
- I read pretty much everything.

00:04:50.383 --> 00:04:52.344
And I just say, you can pretty much tell

00:04:52.344 --> 00:04:53.681
where somebody's head was at.

00:04:53.681 --> 00:04:57.768
But I've never taken any
advice from an article

00:04:57.768 --> 00:04:59.339
that I've read, 'cause like I said,

00:04:59.339 --> 00:05:00.335
I feel like I'm an artist.

00:05:00.335 --> 00:05:01.876
And if you read ...

00:05:01.876 --> 00:05:04.772
An artist, the best
picture I think is like

00:05:04.772 --> 00:05:05.855
the first thing they did.

00:05:05.855 --> 00:05:06.984
Then critics come around and say,

00:05:06.984 --> 00:05:08.429
"If you had done the eyes different ..."

00:05:08.429 --> 00:05:10.194
And then next time you paint, you go,

00:05:10.194 --> 00:05:12.842
"They didn't like the
eyes, so I should ..."

00:05:12.842 --> 00:05:14.937
And I'm not, I just do my thing.

00:05:14.937 --> 00:05:15.770
I've been

00:05:17.537 --> 00:05:19.536
the class clown

00:05:19.536 --> 00:05:21.268
since I was a little kid.

00:05:21.268 --> 00:05:23.438
I started out as a class
clown, and from class clown,

00:05:23.438 --> 00:05:25.104
I went to the school clown.

00:05:25.104 --> 00:05:27.401
From the school clown, I went
to the neighborhood clown,

00:05:27.401 --> 00:05:29.147
and like now, everybody knows me.

00:05:29.147 --> 00:05:30.738
I'm the guy who ...

00:05:30.738 --> 00:05:32.352
I'm Funny Murphy.

00:05:32.352 --> 00:05:33.999
- Put your pants up, that's number one.

00:05:33.999 --> 00:05:35.682
I don't want any of this, right?

00:05:35.682 --> 00:05:38.133
- You know, if I was faced
with choosing another career,

00:05:38.133 --> 00:05:39.772
I think I'd go crazy.

00:05:39.772 --> 00:05:41.666
There's nothing else I could do.

00:05:41.666 --> 00:05:42.632
I decided at a very ...

00:05:42.632 --> 00:05:45.067
I'm 19 now, I decided when I was 17

00:05:45.067 --> 00:05:47.570
that I wanted to go into this, for real.

00:05:47.570 --> 00:05:50.503
And I was familiar with stand-up
comedy and entertainment

00:05:50.503 --> 00:05:51.637
since I was 15.

00:05:51.637 --> 00:05:54.386
A lot of kids tell their
parents they want to be doctors

00:05:54.386 --> 00:05:56.028
and lawyers and garbage like that,

00:05:56.028 --> 00:05:57.331
but I wanted to be a stand-up comedian.

00:05:57.331 --> 00:05:58.475
I told my parents that,

00:05:58.475 --> 00:06:01.427
and everything's working out for me fine.

00:06:01.427 --> 00:06:03.247
I'm growing constantly on the stage,

00:06:03.247 --> 00:06:04.667
and everything's working out for me.

00:06:04.667 --> 00:06:07.509
- I like very much the imitations you did,

00:06:07.509 --> 00:06:08.722
the impressions were great.

00:06:08.722 --> 00:06:10.827
- I want to get ...

00:06:10.827 --> 00:06:14.561
I'll say famous by the
time I'm 21, I'm 19 now.

00:06:14.561 --> 00:06:15.965
I give myself two years.

00:06:15.965 --> 00:06:18.789
I do a little exercise, you
know, just to keep it fit, and

00:06:18.789 --> 00:06:22.234
you know, but more than
anything, it's have a, know the,

00:06:22.234 --> 00:06:24.169
the least amount of, that's the ...

00:06:24.169 --> 00:06:26.714
Stress is really the thing
that really eats you up,

00:06:26.714 --> 00:06:30.600
and I have such a small stress
level, for years and years.

00:06:30.600 --> 00:06:33.298
And when I have something that's stressful

00:06:33.298 --> 00:06:35.354
that I have to deal with,
I've really learned how to

00:06:35.354 --> 00:06:39.084
deal with it and put it in
the back, and not sit around.

00:06:39.084 --> 00:06:43.496
Very rarely, you see me sitting
around the house like this.

00:06:43.496 --> 00:06:46.475
- [Interviewer] You know
it's hard to believe ...

00:06:46.475 --> 00:06:47.726
Yeah of course, you got to.

00:06:47.726 --> 00:06:50.048
- The easier thing is I can tell you

00:06:50.048 --> 00:06:51.760
what's the most gratifying thing.

00:06:51.760 --> 00:06:53.599
The most gratifying
thing for me as an artist

00:06:53.599 --> 00:06:55.349
is to be able to have

00:06:56.471 --> 00:07:01.350
some longevity, and to be able
to connect with an audience.

00:07:01.350 --> 00:07:03.896
Different generations,
to be around for a while,

00:07:03.896 --> 00:07:07.304
especially, you know,
in a business where ...

00:07:07.304 --> 00:07:10.049
People come and go so fast
in the movie business.

00:07:10.049 --> 00:07:13.946
Just to be able to connect
with an audience, you know,

00:07:13.946 --> 00:07:16.624
when you were 19, and you
can still connect with them,

00:07:16.624 --> 00:07:18.872
people still appreciate what you do.

00:07:18.872 --> 00:07:20.954
That's the most gratifying thing.

00:07:20.954 --> 00:07:22.043
Bless you, Paul.

00:07:22.043 --> 00:07:23.444
That's the most gratifying thing.

00:07:23.444 --> 00:07:25.198
